{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DM9", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-picard-stack}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6092a1e02cac8d13d44691deeddac1c93c6a10e77e502c73a6b9fddaed6fdf81", "source_text": "Properties of the Picard stack", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3fead41b507427ae0daefb9e2888db363f5a386ba27f18a8f04955955418d87f", "unit_id": "tag:0DM9:title"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DM9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B}$", "MATH_0003": "$X/B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-proposition-pic}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b360b172bb19e2e06f5ac793c19fce6110996e847e79a778a0024a6d29d81f35", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cba8ca9c1f020699183dc6b93b3f46d366d01c7ecf779ef7fb872a9b3ce35a62", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic spaces which is flat,\nproper, and of finite presentation. Then the stack\n<MATH_0002> parametrizing invertible sheaves on <MATH_0003>\nis algebraic, see Quot, Proposition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:796a81ed9c27dbad58ceaafe66dcc94d6c96220ce2332e39d7ff09765b32f5ac", "unit_id": "tag:0DM9:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DM9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B}$", "MATH_0002": "$B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pic-diagonal-affine-fp}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:058bcb40731742d86cf912b792febca84e15d571558982c24e3a5a4be3e25c91", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a92e3f35870fb2b4868453b1350fcb3d9cd2a2168546d960bc43a2eee8e3b763", "source_text": "The diagonal of <MATH_0001> over <MATH_0002> is affine\nand of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:90699b039ada020b59f55c775c8a69db8b537f658ef6861e5a86d4f2d0fca048", "unit_id": "tag:0DMA:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DM9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Cohstack_{X/B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-lemma-picard-stack-open-in-coh}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-coherent-diagonal-affine-fp}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7bf1e44c66bfd310c2ae0035ac4f112685d563862329ab11252eceefd282579b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d41d183147bc9964ec6e343c7a297392073239034afd37c9cd8227aab5fa06ac", "source_text": "In Quot, Lemma <REF_0001> we have seen that\n<MATH_0001> is an open substack of\n<MATH_0002>. Hence this follows from\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c76f3b1197dbe9e7bd6b365edda9d2d3204dcc34a540425ee73b2384667215b8", "unit_id": "tag:0DMA:proof"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DM9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B} \\to B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pic-qs-lfp}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0c96f1c882aaee2cf58080a208a4f768ea53381baf6f54e999107ad153b7d8e7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6c4b483fed6a925684b01a0cdc6aa125d9c5ab8576705c2299895a73ceb3824e", "source_text": "The morphism <MATH_0001> is quasi-separated and\nlocally of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d247279dea57e3b75173d3b1b9d3388de47d1b19f70e8576a1e81ff047a93078", "unit_id": "tag:0DMB:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DM9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Cohstack_{X/B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-lemma-picard-stack-open-in-coh}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-coherent-qs-lfp}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7bf1e44c66bfd310c2ae0035ac4f112685d563862329ab11252eceefd282579b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7f69746a67e83624bbecab2001be031aa01004810e1c51eea8ff0b47d2c4e35b", "source_text": "In Quot, Lemma <REF_0001> we have seen that\n<MATH_0001> is an open substack of\n<MATH_0002>. Hence this follows from\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c76f3b1197dbe9e7bd6b365edda9d2d3204dcc34a540425ee73b2384667215b8", "unit_id": "tag:0DMB:proof"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DM9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B} \\to B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-morphisms-definition-existence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pic-existence-part}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5ff8c4499ed97e696499dfb1c348d2250ce7e40e0546687e5ae766e276ed755c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f9462e479cccfecb5746b2a733d008f1e8451f2500428618f20c488680251743", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is smooth in addition to being proper.\nThen <MATH_0002> satisfies the existence part\nof the valuative criterion (Morphisms of Stacks, Definition\n<REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5c18924cb517292e671c377092aadca810d63180457f7c2da42767a171c08b50", "unit_id": "tag:0DNG:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DM9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$K$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$R$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_K}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{L}_K$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{L}_K$", "MATH_0010": "$X_K$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{L}_K$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_K}(D_K)$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_K}(D'_K)$", "MATH_0014": "$D_K, D'_K$", "MATH_0015": "$X_K$", "MATH_0016": "$D_K$", "MATH_0017": "$D'_K$", "MATH_0018": "$D, D' \\subset X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-finite-presentation-noetherian}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-over-fields-lemma-smooth-regular}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-divisors-lemma-Noetherian-regular-separated-pic-effective-Cartier}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-divisors-lemma-smooth-over-valuation-ring-effective-Cartier}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:202cb14f7d64b42a039ee8ed4fc5ae6f7898d7224fe8277504f1731aefec2fc7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b5527a8b385c9099705eb74151be13c4508e27e534970e3097a10beac57102d6", "source_text": "Taking base change, this immediately reduces to the following\nproblem: given a valuation ring <MATH_0001> with fraction field <MATH_0002> and\nan algebraic space <MATH_0003> proper and smooth over <MATH_0004> and an invertible\n<MATH_0005>-module <MATH_0006>, show there exists\nan invertible <MATH_0007>-module <MATH_0008>\nwhose generic fibre is <MATH_0009>.\nObserve that <MATH_0010> is Noetherian, separated, and regular\n(use Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nand\nSpaces over Fields, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nThus we can write\n<MATH_0011> as the difference in the Picard group of\n<MATH_0012> and <MATH_0013>\nfor two effective Cartier divisors <MATH_0014> in <MATH_0015>, see\nDivisors on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0003>.\nFinally, we know that <MATH_0016> and <MATH_0017> are restrictions of\neffective Cartier divisors <MATH_0018>, see\nDivisors on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c21638eebebc8151f978a80f3f025fb02d1a0dfb44fe85bccab95ff6a21c1700", "unit_id": "tag:0DNG:proof"}
